  "summary": {
    "as": "Reported to Senate",
    "asOf": "2025-10-27",
    "date": "2026-07-29T12:07:42Z",
    "text": "Shenandoah Mountain Act\n\nThis bill establishes the Shenandoah Mountain National Scenic Area, consisting of approximately 92,562 acres of National Forest System land in Virginia in the George Washington\u00a0and Jefferson National Forest.\n\nThe bill designates specified lands in the forest\u00a0as wilderness and as components of the National Wilderness Preservation System, including approximately (1)\u00a05,088 acres as the\u00a0Skidmore Fork Wilderness, (2)\u00a03,568 acres as the\u00a0Lynn Hollow Wilderness, (3)\u00a012,461 acres as the\u00a0Little River Wilderness, and (4)\u00a05,779 acres as the\u00a0Beech Lick Knob Wilderness. It also incorporates approximately 6,961 acres\u00a0into the Ramseys Draft Wilderness."
  },
